      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a very late bump, but I'd really like this feature still.\n\nThe only way to emulate this requires modifying the rig, or unpacking the avatar prefab. Both of these techniques add some dummy parent object for the component to go on. The former option is not convenient for those unfamiliar with modelling tools, and the latter option can cause problems later on such as if the model is changed. Both of these require constraints.\n\nEdit: Specifically, this targets the use case where the two roots don't share a parent. For instance, ribbons under each arm that have the exact same physbone settings. The ignore list, albeit in a way that feels kind of janky, can be used to achieve multi-root behavior where the parent is shared.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
